What is flexbox

👉Flexbox is a layout model for arranging items (horizontally or vertically)
 within a container, in a flexible and responsive way.

👉Flexbox makes it easy to design a flexible
 and responsive layout, without using float or positioning.

 👉CSS Flexbox is used for a one-dimensional layout, with rows OR columns.

👉CSS Grid is used for a two-dimensional layout, with rows AND columns.

Flex properties
----------------------------
 1️⃣display:flex

 2️⃣ flex-direction : row,row-reverse, column, column reverse
 3️⃣ align-items:center,left,right,algin-self:center

 4️⃣justify-content:     (spacebetween,around,space evenly)(flexstart,flexend,center)

 5️⃣ flex-wrap    ----->wrap,no-wrap,wrap-reverse

 6️⃣ flex-basis(style: flex-basis:250px)
 7️⃣ flex-grow   (increase)
 8️⃣ flex-shrink (decrease)